{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's perception and actuation capabilities, separating sensing (uncontrollable events) from motion (controllable events). The specification enforces safe, progress-oriented exploration: move forward or random_walk in clear, react conservatively to obstacles, recover quickly, and avoid repeated or unsafe actions. Recovery from obstacle_front uses a brief move_backward, then a directed turn; left/right obstacles trigger a directed turn away. The design ensures the robot does not remain in recovery or turning states longer than needed and returns to exploration as soon as the path is clear.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for perception and motion, with all events as specified.",
    "Specification automaton encodes safe, progress-maximizing exploration with conservative, minimal recovery and rapid return to forward motion."
